; Compiled with the sarek_matrix alert promoted to an ERROR, so this stanza is
; itself a gate: a negative kernel that the PPX advises (a false positive) or a
; positive kernel whose [@alert "-sarek_matrix"] / [@@alert "-sarek_matrix"]
; does not silence the advice fails the BUILD. The test then checks the
; recognised roles, layouts and rejection reasons at run time.

(test
 (name test_matrix_pattern)
 (modules test_matrix_pattern)
 (libraries sarek sarek_stdlib sarek_ir alcotest astring fmt)
 (preprocess
  (pps sarek_ppx))
 (flags
  (:standard -w -33 -alert @sarek_matrix)))
